EE timer 0: PS2X_TIMER0=frame makes what the guest reads from the count independent of emulated time. Each read returns a hash of how many times the count has been written (a game resets it once a frame) and of the read's place since then, in 0x100 to 0x10FF; the timer keeps counting underneath, so its interrupts and compare matches are unchanged. Metropolismania takes the count as a random number (people's destinations, sound noise), so with the switch two runs whose code takes different time (the readable port against the recompiled code, a native renderer against the emulated one) make the same choices and can be compared state for state. PS2X_TIMER0_TRACE=1 also prints how many reads the guest made between writes, which shows a run that reads the count more or fewer times than another. Off by default.

